{
  "assessment": "This change introduces `solution.mjs` as a new file containing an intersection function that relies on two nested `.includes()` calls inside a loop, failing to implement the required optimization for roughly linear time. The code correctly computes the result but retains O(N×M) complexity instead of using Sets or hash maps for lookups, which will cause severe performance degradation on larger inputs.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Execution scales quadratically; the nested `.includes()` calls cause CPU time to spike dramatically on arrays larger than a few hundred elements.",
      "at": "solution.mjs",
      "call": "`node -e \"const {intersection} = require('./solution.mjs'); const a = Array.from({length: 3000}, (_, i) => i); console.time('perf_test'); intersection(a, a); console.timeEnd('perf_test');\"`",
      "defect": "Quadratic time complexity due to repeated array scanning instead of O(1) lookups.",
      "expected": "Execution completes almost instantly (milliseconds), with runtime scaling linearly as input size increases."
    }
  ]
}
